head - print the beginning of input

SYNOPSIS
    head [-count] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Print the first count lines of each file or, with no file operands, of
    standard input. The default count is 10. Supply count as a positive
    decimal number preceded by a dash.

EXAMPLES
    head -5 /README

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), tail(1), wc(1)
